Spatial navigation: no style and layout update per element in the candidate walk.

FindNextCandidateInContainer() checks every element with IsKeyboardFocusableSlow(), whose default
UpdateBehavior::kStyleAndLayout makes CanBeKeyboardFocusableScroller() call Document::UpdateStyleAndLayoutForNode()
for each non-link element. On a Wikipedia article (11 672 elements walked) that is about 3 750 Document::
UpdateStyleAndLayout calls per arrow key on the LG C1, about 130 of the 170 ms of a Down press.
On a clean document such a call changes nothing, except under a locked display lock (content-visibility: auto,
54 locks on that page), where it forces the locked subtree up to date. The walk now updates once, forces once per
lock (its first element), and checks the rest with kNoneForFocusManagement. If a forced update leaves the document
dirty, the rest of the walk takes the old per-element path, so the candidates stay the same. A trace event
(blink, SpatialNavigation::CandidateWalk) reports elements, forced updates and whether the document stayed clean.
Not fixed in Chromium main as of 2026-11-18 (the same calls in spatial_navigation_controller.cc and element.cc).

